<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Where dost Thou, dear Shepherd, resort with Thy sheep,</l><l>To feed them in pastures of love;</l><l>Say, why in the valley of death should I weep,</l><l>Or alone in this wilderness rove?</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Oh, why should I wander, an alien from Thee,</l><l>Or cry in the desert for bread?</l><l>Thy foes will rejoice when my sorrows they see,</l><l>And smile at the tears I have shed.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Ye daughters of Zion, declare, have you seen</l><l>The Star that on Israel shone?</l><l>Say, if in your tents my Beloved has been,</l><l>And where with His flocks He is gone.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Dear Shepherd! I hear, and will follow Thy call;</l><l>I know the sweet sound of Thy voice;</l><l>Restore and defend me, for Thou art my all,</l><l>And in Thee I’ll ever rejoice.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
